{"created": "2026-09-14T13:44:49.636245+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-14T13:44:50.584161+00:00", "id": 22036773, "conceptrecid": "22036772", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22036773", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22036772", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22036773", "metadata": {"title": "Irrigation of Kherson and Zaporizhzhia 2019 - 2025", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22036773", "publication_date": "2026-08-21", "description": "<p>The ongoing war in Ukraine has drawn international attention to the impact of conflict on global agricultural production and food security. On June 6, 2023, the Kakhovka Dam was destroyed. The loss of this critical agricultural and energy infrastructure has left most farmers on the East bank of the Dnipro River without irrigation in Kherson and Zaporizhzhia oblasts. This study develops a multi-sensor Earth Observation framework combining high resolution satellite imagery (Sentinel-2, Landsat) with meteorological data (CHIRPS) and water productivity data (FAO WaPOR), using a semi-supervised machine learning pipeline.</p>\n<p>The dataset presented here is of classifier irrigated fields in Kherson and Zaporizhzhia oblasts for 2019 - 2025.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Accompanying the manuscript under review at Frontiers in Remote Sensing.&nbsp;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Baber, Sheila", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0002-5596-8970"}, {"name": "Skakun, Sergii", "affiliation": "University of Maryland, College Park", "orcid": "0000-0002-9039-0174"}, {"name": "Sadeh, Yuval", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0002-4346-0432"}, {"name": "Shumilo, Leonid", "affiliation": "University of Maryland, College Park", "orcid": "0000-0002-7395-7933"}, {"name": "Oliinyk, Oleksandra", "affiliation": "University of Maryland, College Park"}, {"name": "Hosseini, Mehdi", "affiliation": "University of Maryland"}, {"name": "Wagner, Josef", "affiliation": "Universit\u00e9 de Strasbourg", "orcid": "0009-0000-3470-5752"}, {"name": "Khan, Abdul Qadir", "